  "notes": [
    "Development venue for the app until the three real venues ship (#83). Not a v1.0 venue.",
    "Venue frame: metres, x east, y north. Directions are compass bearings in degrees. Schema: docs/venue-file.md.",
    "Open water with a shore strip beyond each side of the race area, a small headland on the west shore, no current.",
    "Every pairing is laid from the start line centre at the origin with the mean wind from the north, like the prototype's course.",
    "Conditions refs are the four bundled conditions files at version 3 (#221, #233): faster shifts, a readable wobble and a wider puff fan. Version 3 differs from version 2, and version 2 from version 1 (the schema-2 files, #75, #77), only in those refs and this note.",
    "Geographic grids are a gentle placeholder shore effect: up to 3 deg of bend and 12 % shadow at each shoreline, nearly neutral mid-course.",
    "Landmark asset names are placeholders until docs/assets-manifest.md (#53).",
    "Version 4 (#286) is version 3 with its conditions refs at version 4, the schema-3 files with a pressure field (ADR 0008). The pressure field is laid across an across-the-wind coordinate derived at load from each pairing's geographic grid, so nothing else changes.",
    "Version 5 (schema 2, #287, ADR 0008) is version 4 with the venue's geography authored to be seen in play, on the version-5 conditions files (schema 4), which say how much it steers the pressure field. Each pairing's grid gives a signed speed change in place of the speed factor: up to 11 % more pressure in a band off the west headland (x about -300 m, 400 m off its tip, inside the race area), running down the course from the headland and fading upwind of it, a shadow band of up to 19 % less under the east shore (x 300 m on), and the old shadow on the west shore itself. Lane spots (lanePreference) lie along the same band off the headland. A mild left-side tendency (sideTendency 0.06: the west, the left of the course looking upwind into the northerly) leans the pressure side that way in most races. Bends, land, landmarks and everything else are version 4's. Placeholders, like the grids before them, until the real venues (#83) teach what reads well.",
    "Version 6 (#288) is version 5 with its conditions refs at version 6, the schema-5 files whose puffs and lulls form from the pressure field at about a third of the old coverage. Everything else is version 5's.",
    "Version 7 (#288 follow-up, ADR 0008) is version 6 with its conditions refs at version 7, the schema-6 files whose pressure lanes are finite, drifting, sometimes weak patches and whose pressure side is weaker. The geography is version 6's; the lane spots now draw a smaller share of the lanes."
  ],
